    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Let $p$ be a solution of the equation $x^6-2=0$. Then the value of $(p-1)(p^{12}+p^{13}+\\cdots+p^{41})$ is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "124"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "144"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "192"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "212"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "252"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Telescoping product",
        "body": "$(p-1)(p^{12}+p^{13}+\\cdots+p^{41})=p^{42}-p^{12}$ (every middle term cancels). Since $p^6=2$: $p^{42}=(p^6)^7=2^7=128$ and $p^{12}=(p^6)^2=4$. The value is $128-4=124$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 124**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "algebra",
      "sequences-series"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
