    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "If $m$ and $n$ are natural numbers such that $\\sqrt{7+\\sqrt{48}}=\\sqrt m+\\sqrt n$ then $m^2+n^2$ equals",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "25"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "37"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "29"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "40"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "41"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Square both sides",
        "body": "$7+\\sqrt{48}=m+n+2\\sqrt{mn}$. Matching, $m+n=7$ and $mn=12$, so $\\{m,n\\}=\\{3,4\\}$ and $m^2+n^2=9+16=25$. (Indeed $(\\sqrt3+\\sqrt4)^2=7+2\\sqrt{12}=7+\\sqrt{48}$.)\n\n**Answer: (A) 25**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "algebra"
