    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "$ABCD$ is a trapezium with $AD$ parallel to $BC$. The diagonals $AC$ and $BD$ intersect at $O$. If the area of triangle $AOD$ is $x$, and the area of triangle $BOC$ is $y$, then the area of the trapezium is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$2(x+y)$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$4\\sqrt{xy}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac{8xy}{x+y}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)^2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "None of these."
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Areas of the four triangles",
        "body": "Triangles $AOD$ and $COB$ are similar, so $\\dfrac{DO}{OB}=\\dfrac{AO}{OC}$. Triangles with the same height have areas proportional to their bases: $\\dfrac{DO}{OB}=\\dfrac{[AOD]}{[AOB]}$ and $\\dfrac{AO}{OC}=\\dfrac{[AOB]}{[BOC]}$. Hence $\\dfrac x{[AOB]}=\\dfrac{[AOB]}y$, so $[AOB]=\\sqrt{xy}$, and similarly $[DOC]=\\sqrt{xy}$. The trapezium has area $x+y+2\\sqrt{xy}=(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)^2$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $(\\sqrt x+\\sqrt y)^2$**"
      }
    ],
