        "title": "Split into odd and even denominators",
        "body": "Let $t=1+\\frac1{3^2}+\\frac1{5^2}+\\cdots$ (reciprocals of odd squares). The even-denominator terms are $\\frac1{2^2}+\\frac1{4^2}+\\cdots=\\frac14\\left(1+\\frac1{2^2}+\\frac1{3^2}+\\cdots\\right)=\\frac14s$. Since $s$ is the sum of both kinds of terms, $s=t+\\frac14s$, so $t=\\frac34s$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac34s$**"
