        "text": "$\\frac1{1999}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac1{4000}$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Auxiliary polynomial",
        "body": "Let $Q(x)=xP(x)-1$. It has degree 1999 and $Q(k)=0$ for $k=1,\\dots,1999$, so $Q(x)=C(x-1)(x-2)\\cdots(x-1999)$. At $x=0$: $Q(0)=-1=C(-1)^{1999}\\,1999!$, so $C=\\dfrac1{1999!}$. Then $Q(2000)=\\dfrac{1999!}{1999!}=1=2000P(2000)-1$, so $P(2000)=\\dfrac2{2000}=\\dfrac1{1000}$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $\\frac1{1000}$**"
      }
    ],
